# What must never enter the runner's build context.
#
# The build context is the repo root, which on the host is /opt/ghostclick —
# the same directory the deploy script requires .env.prod to live in, the same
# directory docs/DEPLOY.md tells you to put cansee-deploy.pem in, and the
# parent of .ghostclick/. `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would put all three into
# an image layer, where `docker history` reads them back out. Today that is
# contained only by the fact that the image never leaves the box; it stops
# being contained the moment anything is pushed to a registry.
#
# This is a correctness file, not a size optimisation.

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.prod.example
*.pem
*.key
# The vault, the origin allowlist, the run history, the shared secret.
.ghostclick/

# --- the dev tree ----------------------------------------------------------
# `COPY . .` runs AFTER `npm ci --omit=dev`, so a context carrying node_modules
# overwrites the production install with the full development one — a bundler
# and a second Chromium download shipped to production, silently.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
# Built in stage 1 and copied from there. The committed copy is for `npm start`
# on a laptop and is not what the image should serve.
web/dist/

# --- history ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded on purpose. The commit reaches the image as the GC_GIT_SHA build
# argument instead — see the identity block in server.js.
.git/
.github/
.claude/

# --- not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------------
# auth/ is the control plane and builds from its own context (../auth), so it
# is dead weight here and its db.sqlite3 is a real account database.
auth/
docs/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Kept deliberately, despite being tempting to exclude: scripts/, suites/,
# public/ and extension/ are what `npm run check:all` needs, and DEPLOY.md
# documents running exactly that inside the container.
